//@version=6
// CSI CYCLE_reduced — REDUCED Pine variant. STATUS: NOT_COMPILED_IN_TRADINGVIEW, NOT_BACKTESTED_IN_TV, NOT_PARITY_WITH_PYTHON.
// Inputs lost vs the Python CYCLE model: MVRV / MVRV-Z, Puell Multiple, mcap/thermocap, realized-cap change, hash ribbons,
// fee share, exchange supply ratio, mcap per active address (none are available as equivalent TradingView symbols).
// What remains: price-only valuation stretch on the chart symbol. Score = mean of causal percentile ranks (1 = expensive).
// Non-repainting: uses only closed daily bars (barstate.isconfirmed) and no lookahead in request.security.
indicator("CSI CYCLE_reduced (research-only)", overlay=false, max_bars_back=5000)
// percent rank uses a rolling window (ta.percentrank), unlike the Python expanding percentile: values differ by construction
mayer   = close / ta.sma(close, 200)
ma2y    = close / ta.sma(close, 730)
ma200w  = close / ta.sma(close, 1400) - 1
// causal percentile rank of the current value within its own past
f_pct(src, n) =>
    ta.percentrank(src, n) / 100.0
lookback = 1500
p1 = f_pct(mayer, lookback)
p2 = f_pct(ma2y, lookback)
p3 = f_pct(ma200w, lookback)
score = (nz(p1) + nz(p2) + nz(p3)) / (1 * (na(p1) ? 0 : 1) + (na(p2) ? 0 : 1) + (na(p3) ? 0 : 1))
plot(barstate.isconfirmed ? score : na, "CYCLE_reduced score (1 = expensive)", color=color.orange)
hline(0.5)
alertcondition(score > 0.9, "CYCLE_reduced high", "CYCLE_reduced score > 0.9 (research-only; not a trade instruction)")
alertcondition(score < 0.1, "CYCLE_reduced low", "CYCLE_reduced score < 0.1 (research-only; not a trade instruction)")
